{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q1991431","formula":"K₂NaFe₇Ti₂Si₈O₂₈(OH)₄F","hill":"FFe7H4K2NaO32Si8Ti2","elements":["H","O","F","Na","Si","K","Ti","Fe"],"composition":{"F":1.0,"H":4.0,"K":2.0,"O":32.0,"Fe":7.0,"Na":1.0,"Si":8.0,"Ti":2.0},"names":{"en":"Astrophyllite","ru":"Астрофиллит","uk":"Астрофіліт"},"descriptions":{"en":"Astrophyllite is a very rare, brown to golden-yellow hydrous potassium iron titanium silicate mineral. Belonging to the astrophyllite group, astrophyllite may be classed either as an inosilicate, phyllosilicate, or an intermediate between the two. It forms an isomorphous series with kupletskite, to which it is visually identical and often intimately associated.","ru":"Астрофилли́т — минерал класса силикатов, титаноцирконосиликат с комбинированной слоисто-ленточной кристаллической структурой. Назван от греческого слова «астра» — звезда. Образует включённые в породу удлинённо-пластинчатые кристаллы и эффектные звёздчатые, спутанно-волокнистые или параллельно-волокнистые агрегаты.","uk":"Астрофіліт (рос. астрофиллит; англ. astrophyllite; нім."},"fame":22,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":null,"structure":null,"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1991431","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Astrophyllite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%90%D1%81%D1%82%D1%80%D0%BE%D1%84%D0%B8%D0%BB%D0%BB%D0%B8%D1%82","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (uk)","url":"https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%90%D1%81%D1%82%D1%80%D0%BE%D1%84%D1%96%D0%BB%D1%96%D1%82","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"photo","name":"Wikimedia Commons","url":"https://commons.wikime